    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0665" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d262-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-03">3 August 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Former Naval Person to President. Personal and most secret. Number 398.</p>
                <p>War Cabinet think that the time for negotiating about Rome being an open city has
                    passed. Surely there would be the utmost danger that any such bargain would
                    encourage the Italians to make a try on for a neutralization of Italy itself.
                    Anyhow, that is the way it would be viewed here.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d262-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d262-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission to Washington not indicated. Forwarded by the White House
                    Map Room to Roosevelt, who was then at Birch Island. An information copy was
                    sent to Hull on August 3, 1943, by the Secretary of the Joint Chiefs of Staff
                    (Deane) (740.0011 EW/8–343).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
